name: registry-drift
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: |
  Fires when a diagnostic code is emitted but never declared in the
  ErrorCode enum — the emit exists, the registry doesn't know it.
  stdlib-side diagnostics are the usual suspect: koru_std prints
  `error[KORUnnn]` as formatted text, bypassing the typed emit path,
  so the enum discipline can only be enforced after the fact by the
  registry-coherence watcher.

  Witnessed 2026-10-23: 7b540681c made a second `std/kernel:step`
  refuse with KORU127 via std.debug.print in kernel.kz but never
  declared the code; the watcher's ORPHAN_EMIT caught it on the full
  ceremony, and the drain was a one-line enum declaration.
route: surface
